Clear the rollback index of each sequence that the recurrent memory removes
Fold-into: upstream/memory

The defects. tests/fuzz/core/run.sh test replays the reproducer of each one.

- The removal of a sequence keeps its pending rollback index.

  seq_keep removes the other sequences, and seq_rm of a range that removes the last cell of a
  sequence removes it, but the two keep the pending rollback index rs_idx of that sequence (and
  its depth). The next decode of the sequence then reads its first state from a snapshot group
  of an old state. seq_rm(s, -1, -1) and seq_rm(s, 0, -1) clear the index.

  The change: The two paths clear rs_idx and rs_depth of each sequence that they remove.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_recurrent--recurrent-keep-rollback.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

